{"id": "EUVD-2026-103665", "enisaUuid": "a250664f-8937-3b70-b94a-a9ad046dd66a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: unregister net_devices in case of probe failure\n\nIf register_netdev() fails for one of the MTK_MAX_DEVS devices in\nmtk_probe(), the error path jumps to err_deinit_ppe, skipping\nmtk_unreg_dev(). The previously registered net_devices are then freed by\nmtk_free_dev() while still in NETREG_REGISTERED state, hitting the\nBUG_ON(dev->reg_state != NETREG_UNREGISTERED).\n\nRoute the register_netdev() failure to err_unreg_netdev so the net_devices\nregistered so far are properly unregistered before being freed.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:48", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/245bea0c7ab278150c70366bdeb69b901327133c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab3bde3b3e56331b4f53a1f6cf4e5e9d1c14c1a0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7254b702e556158e34b4d7c168b5d8e7da5978af", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0fdb944d4df02223c67d5e65c4c134ecb57a5668", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/310d1ac61a4d5a2ca8356a3a48d263acf54503ce"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98620", "GHSA-gfj4-2pq5-q7vj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3788ec45-3e41-3e9d-b8e5-e38945707255", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a8a9e89f801ce5d3d1d57ac48db678caf072147 <310d1ac61a4d5a2ca8356a3a48d263acf54503ce"}, {"id": "3b097036-14bd-3a89-817c-2e3273e13083", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "558f9884-c594-314a-9bc6-49060a1ef5a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "7652129a-8af5-320a-b22f-1840f46a3b64", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a8a9e89f801ce5d3d1d57ac48db678caf072147 <ab3bde3b3e56331b4f53a1f6cf4e5e9d1c14c1a0"}, {"id": "7e65e065-6d83-3c27-b290-618d1ef4bc76", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "a0f060a4-b5ef-380a-9a52-1269b6162ee6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a8a9e89f801ce5d3d1d57ac48db678caf072147 <7254b702e556158e34b4d7c168b5d8e7da5978af"}, {"id": "a34952f2-1fdc-34a3-92a8-71a54f636080", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a8a9e89f801ce5d3d1d57ac48db678caf072147 <245bea0c7ab278150c70366bdeb69b901327133c"}, {"id": "a60530d3-cae5-33c9-82b0-96e56a5be425", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a8a9e89f801ce5d3d1d57ac48db678caf072147 <0fdb944d4df02223c67d5e65c4c134ecb57a5668"}, {"id": "c8154b44-ed5c-3bdc-ba37-ff1134439aac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.9"}, {"id": "d7294708-8702-3d04-bdfd-277e462aa0e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e7bdb0fe-67e5-3214-b189-3b36c4ba5bee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "edae8701-f894-3f4c-82df-226cecba7f52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9d45bcd7-097c-38b4-a5a0-1760e1c5b789", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}